Astro Incremental Static Builds 導入準備
Astro 7.2 upgrade error excerpts
Recorded: 2026-08-29 JST

These are excerpts, not complete command outputs.
Local user and repository path segments are replaced with <repo> or <user-library>.

======================================================================
CASE 1: stale node_modules prevented the baseline build
Command: pnpm run build
Result: exit 1
Category: local dependency installation state
Not evidence of: Astro 7.2 incompatibility
======================================================================

[astro] Unable to load your Astro config

Cannot find module '@astrojs/markdown-remark' imported from '<repo>/astro.config.mjs'

ELIFECYCLE Command failed with exit code 1.

Abstract meaning:
The manifest and lockfile declared a package that the current node_modules tree did not contain.
The build could not reach application compilation because config loading failed first.

======================================================================
CASE 2: repository supply-chain policy rejected a very recent release
Command: pnpm add 'astro@^7.2.9'
Result: exit 1
Category: dependency release-age policy
Not evidence of: package absence or semver incompatibility
======================================================================

ERR_PNPM_NO_MATURE_MATCHING_VERSION Version 7.2.9 (released 37 hours ago) of astro does not meet the minimumReleaseAge constraint

The latest release of astro is "7.2.9". Published at 8/28/2026

Abstract meaning:
Astro 7.2.9 existed, but the repository intentionally refused packages published less than 72 hours earlier.
The safe response was to select a mature 7.2 release, not to add an exception merely to obtain the newest patch.

Decision:
Use Astro 7.2.7, which had passed the configured 4320-minute release-age threshold.

======================================================================
CASE 3: Astro and Markdown integration versions were not aligned
Command: pnpm add 'astro@7.2.7'
Result: install succeeded with peer warning
Category: integration compatibility
======================================================================

WARN Issues with peer dependencies found
.
├─┬ astro 7.2.7
│ └── ✕ unmet peer @astrojs/markdown-remark@7.2.4: found 7.2.1
└─┬ eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y 6.10.2
  └── ✕ unmet peer eslint@"^3 || ^4 || ^5 || ^6 || ^7 || ^8 || ^9": found 10.7.0

Abstract meaning:
The Astro core update completed, but its exact Markdown Remark peer version was not satisfied.
The JSX accessibility warning was pre-existing and unrelated to Astro Incremental Static Builds.

Decision:
Update @astrojs/markdown-remark to 7.2.4 and @astrojs/mdx to 7.0.8.
Keep @astrojs/cloudflare 14.1.4 and Wrangler 4.112.0 because their declared peer ranges already accepted Astro 7.2.7.

