CASE 6: the first dev-server startup exited before readiness
Command: pnpm run dev
Initial result: exit 1
Category: Astro background dev-server cold startup
Not evidence of: removed API or Cloudflare adapter incompatibility
======================================================================

{"message":"Dev server process exited before becoming ready.","label":"SKIP_FORMAT","level":"error"}
ELIFECYCLE Command failed with exit code 1.

Background:
Astro detects the Codex agent environment and starts the dev server as a detached background process.
The previously installed local tree used Astro 6.1.1, while the upgraded tree uses Astro 7.2.7.
The background server workflow therefore became observable after dependencies were synchronized.

Diagnostic commands:
astro dev status
astro dev logs
astro dev stop

Verification:
A direct verbose startup succeeded and wrote .astro/dev.json.
The health endpoint returned {"ok":true}.
After a clean stop, the ordinary pnpm run dev command also started successfully.

Successful output:
{"message":"Dev server running at http://localhost:4321 (pid <pid>)\n  Stop:   astro dev stop\n  Status: astro dev status\n  Logs:   astro dev logs","label":"SKIP_FORMAT","level":"info"}

Abstract meaning:
The first cold background startup failed before Astro's readiness check completed.
The same versions started successfully after dependency optimization was warm.
No deprecated project API or integration incompatibility was found.

Current state after diagnosis:
The background dev server is running at http://localhost:4321.

